ModMetaData.description:
A salt-crusted, stilt-rooted mangal forest standing in brackish channels between a dying sea and the rivers that feed it, under a green-gold haze of its own breath.

The biome brings its own living mechanics, each with a switch on the Environmental Hazards Kit's settings screen:
 - a fresh-to-brine salinity gradient that repaints the ground over time;
 - a breath-tide surge that shoves the brine inland, then lets it recede;
 - stranding pools that leave young creatures behind when the tide pulls back;
 - a permanent haze with a low, steady exposure;
 - a small chance that a colonist who survives a disease here comes out of it changed for good: toughened skin, hardened immunity, or something stranger;
 - warden mothers guarding their crèches, and a lasting memory for whoever kills one.

Its canopy is four kinds of mangal, with rainbow blooms, a carnivorous clade that preys on the arthropod floor (never a colonist, never a tame animal), and muck-and-silt plants that yield delta salt and silt. Native creatures include a delta-loam composter and a fever swarm; other animals join from compatible mods when they are installed.

Mod Settings: how often the biome generates on new worlds (0 = never; worldgen-affecting).
